<title>UK: RMC deputy chairman says wants to retire.</title>
<headline>RMC deputy chairman says wants to retire.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The deputy chairman of construction materials manfacturer RMC Group Plc, Leslie Fletcher, said he was keen to retire from his position with effect from December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Fletcher has been a non-executive director of the company since 1983.</p>
<p>In a statement, RMC said it had appointed Karlheinz Rosner, 63, as non-executive director with effect from January 1, 1997.</p>
<p>The company did not say who would succeed Fletcher as deputy chairman.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
